{
    "word": "godlike",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f9c8f921-2f4a-3d95-9653-e95f0dc05865",
                "word": "godlike",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "93c2a97a-de8f-434d-aba9-7f592784d42d",
                        "entry_id": "f9c8f921-2f4a-3d95-9653-e95f0dc05865",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more godlike"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e604cca7-6513-4c15-a202-322d90d35140",
                        "entry_id": "f9c8f921-2f4a-3d95-9653-e95f0dc05865",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most godlike"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "30241339-6b0e-3526-80b0-6f9a8c2e6281",
                        "entry_id": "f9c8f921-2f4a-3d95-9653-e95f0dc05865",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having the characteristics of a god."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "185bd2b5-a02b-48bd-bd0a-95ed5a937723",
                                "sense_id": "30241339-6b0e-3526-80b0-6f9a8c2e6281",
                                "text": "Man himself had been his greatest blunder; he had created a rival to himself; science makes men godlike — it is all up with priests and gods when man becomes scientific!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47a1a9e2-dc77-4811-8519-164712307958",
                                "sense_id": "30241339-6b0e-3526-80b0-6f9a8c2e6281",
                                "text": "When a normal ensign looked at his commander, he ought to see a godlike being, not a, a... future subordinate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e55e5ac-d94a-4f65-8f40-f747a88e08d9",
                                "sense_id": "30241339-6b0e-3526-80b0-6f9a8c2e6281",
                                "text": "Godlike aliens! Man, do I hate godlike aliens! I'll trade a critter for a godlike alien, any day!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5007c6b1-a13a-3262-ae89-b4c33a62d50b",
                        "entry_id": "f9c8f921-2f4a-3d95-9653-e95f0dc05865",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characteristic of a god."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d2aa090-9485-47b4-82d3-08e604862558",
                                "sense_id": "5007c6b1-a13a-3262-ae89-b4c33a62d50b",
                                "text": "And each imagin'd pinnacle and steep / Of godlike hardship tells me I must die / Like a sick Eagle looking at the sky."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0bbca16-dbd8-478e-a3fe-464e1b3f4dba",
                                "sense_id": "5007c6b1-a13a-3262-ae89-b4c33a62d50b",
                                "text": "Beneficence is godlike, and he who does most good to his fellow-man is the Master of Masters, and has learned the Art of Arts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20ab9d4c-46e0-45d7-80d1-3c177dc7c695",
                                "sense_id": "5007c6b1-a13a-3262-ae89-b4c33a62d50b",
                                "text": "It took the combined skills of three great civilizations far apart in time to frame that godlike concept in which the tangible universe itself was only a single factor."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
